  "problem": "If\n    $U=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]$,\nthen find the transpose of $U.$\n\n  \n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n  <tbody><tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"right\">\n      ${U}^{T}=$ \n    </td>\n\n    <td width=\"5px\"></td>\n\n    <td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n      {{field-1}}\n    </td>\n\n    <td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n      {{field-2}}\n    </td>\n    <td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n      {{field-3}}\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td></td>\n\n    <td align=\"center\">\n      {{field-4}}\n    </td>\n\n    <td align=\"center\">\n      {{field-5}}\n    </td>\n    <td align=\"center\">\n      {{field-6}}\n    </td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns:\n\n$$\n{U}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
